**What's going on:** the AI Store was built on the assumption that every `*.agent.md` file is a separate agent, and the sample repositories it was tested with even have two agents in one repository. Your Bitbucket project works differently: **one repository is one agent**, and its extra `.agent.md` files are probably helper agents the main one hands work to. So 84 repositories became 327 agents.

**The fix:** show one agent per repository, using its **main** agent file, and treat the other files as part of that agent. The hard part is deciding which file is the main one, and I can't see your repositories. So the first prompt has Copilot **look at your real data and report back without changing anything**. The second prompt makes the change once you've confirmed the rule.

